<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its November 21 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.93 (13.94)	     14.43  (14.44)</p>
<p>    Six months	    15.39 (15.49)	     16.67  (16.79)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.95 (15.00)	     17.57  (17.64)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 21.26  (21.42)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
